# The LightGBM model dump is read by LightGBM's own text parser, which does
# not tolerate CR: with core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout turns it into
# CRLF and every "Tree=N" marker fails to parse ("Model format error, expect
# a tree here"), taking app/services/ranking.py down at import time.
# Keep it LF in the working tree regardless of the user's autocrlf setting.
backend/app/ml_models/*.txt -text
